      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__system_1gad3cbfe676d6ca096c4a943bbd2ff3b83" prot="public" static="no" nodiscard="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type><ref refid="System_2Export_8hpp_1a6476c9e422606477a4c23d92b1d79a1f" kindref="member">SFML_SYSTEM_API</ref> std::ostream &amp;</type>
        <definition>SFML_SYSTEM_API std::ostream &amp; sf::err</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>err</name>
        <qualifiedname>sf::err</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Standard stream used by SFML to output warnings and errors. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>By default, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__system_1gad3cbfe676d6ca096c4a943bbd2ff3b83" kindref="member">sf::err()</ref></computeroutput> outputs to the same location as <computeroutput>std::cerr</computeroutput>, (-&gt; the stderr descriptor) which is the console if there&apos;s one available.</para>
<para>It is a standard <computeroutput>std::ostream</computeroutput> instance, so it supports all the insertion operations defined by the STL (<computeroutput>operator&lt;&lt;</computeroutput>, manipulators, etc.).</para>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="group__system_1gad3cbfe676d6ca096c4a943bbd2ff3b83" kindref="member">sf::err()</ref></computeroutput> can be redirected to write to another output, independently of <computeroutput>std::cerr</computeroutput>, by using the <computeroutput>rdbuf()</computeroutput> function provided by the <computeroutput>std::ostream</computeroutput> class.</para>
<para>Example: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Redirect<sp/>to<sp/>a<sp/>file</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">std::ofstream<sp/>file(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;sfml-log.txt&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">std::streambuf*<sp/>previous<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__system_1gad3cbfe676d6ca096c4a943bbd2ff3b83" kindref="member">sf::err</ref>().rdbuf(file.rdbuf());</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Redirect<sp/>to<sp/>nothing</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="group__system_1gad3cbfe676d6ca096c4a943bbd2ff3b83" kindref="member">sf::err</ref>().rdbuf(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">nullptr</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Restore<sp/>the<sp/>original<sp/>output</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="group__system_1gad3cbfe676d6ca096c4a943bbd2ff3b83" kindref="member">sf::err</ref>().rdbuf(previous);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Reference to <computeroutput>std::ostream</computeroutput> representing the SFML error stream </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
